1
00:00:00,920 --> 00:00:03,080
 - Don't tell me eating healthy is too expensive.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:07,360
 This lunch at McDonald's just cost me $18.50.

3
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:09,640
 Let me show you how I could make a healthy lunch

4
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:12,200
 at home that would cost far less than that.

5
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,560
 Look at the difference here, guys.

6
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:17,200
 I just made this healthy lunch, grass-fed beef burgers

7
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,880
 with raw cheese, organic chicken, tallow, potato fries,

8
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:25,000
 and fresh squeezed orange juice for about $9.50.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,320
 But wait, Paul, you say,

10
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:28,600
 I don't have time to make this healthy food.

11
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:31,160
 Well, how long did it take you to drive to McDonald's?

12
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:33,080
 And how long did it take you to sit in the drive-through?

13
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:34,600
 And how long did it take you to drive back

14
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,800
 from McDonald's to your job?

15
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,960
 Because making this took me about 25 minutes.

16
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,360
 Think about how much better you're gonna feel

17
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:42,400
 and how much more productivity you're gonna get in your job,

18
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,760
 in your work, in anything you like to do

19
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:45,800
 when you eat more healthfully.

20
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:48,140
 So eating healthfully is an investment, yes,

21
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:50,860
 but it pays off so many dividends in the end.

22
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:52,560
 This is being lazy and this will come back

23
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,600
 to bite you in the ass so quickly.

24
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:55,800
 Put more effort in in the beginning

25
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,080
 and you will thrive long-term.

26
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:58,240
 There's no comparison here.

